WEBVTT

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.600
The first thing you might do with a garter
bar is to remove stitches

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:21.610
from the machine and rehang them.

00:00:21.643 --> 00:00:24.570
I've knit a bit
of stockinette with weight.

00:00:24.603 --> 00:00:27.570
Having weight on the
knitting is important.

00:00:27.603 --> 00:00:33.450
I've pulled the needles all the way out
and make sure all the latches are open.

00:00:33.483 --> 00:00:36.330
Position the garter bar over the needles.

00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:40.170
The hooks of the needles
will go in the slots.

00:00:40.203 --> 00:00:43.930
Gently pull the stitches off
the needles onto the bar.

00:00:43.963 --> 00:00:48.360
As you pull the stitches,
the latches will close and that stitch

00:00:48.393 --> 00:00:52.487
will slip right onto the garter bar.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.520
Now, you'll be nervous the first time you
do this, but with practice,

00:00:55.553 --> 00:00:57.520
it gets easier.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.050
Push the stitches all the way
to the back of the bar,

00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:04.370
and then tilt the bar up,
releasing it from the hooks,

00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:07.690
and remove the knitting from the machine.

00:01:07.723 --> 00:01:12.810
At this point, you could set the work
aside or move the entire piece,

00:01:12.843 --> 00:01:18.650
working increases and decreases,
returning the stitches to the needles.

00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:22.400
To rehang the stitches,
make sure the latches are open and put

00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:25.840
the slots of the bar in the
hooks of the needles again.

00:01:25.873 --> 00:01:30.210
Slide the stitches back onto the needles.

00:01:30.243 --> 00:01:34.360
If you have a needle stopper,
it can secure the needles and make

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:37.810
it easier to rehang the stitches.

00:01:37.843 --> 00:01:43.330
The second way you can use a garter bar is
to remove the knitting from the machine,

00:01:43.363 --> 00:01:50.250
turn it around, rehang the stitches,
and knit a row. Adding purl stitches.

00:01:50.283 --> 00:01:54.690
Although it's not practical to knit
the equivalent of garter stitch this way,

00:01:54.723 --> 00:01:58.640
but just for a few rows,
this could be a real time saver over

00:01:58.673 --> 00:02:03.010
scrapping off or manually
reforming stitches.

00:02:03.043 --> 00:02:07.890
Unlike the vintage style of garter bar
that has hills and valleys,

00:02:07.923 --> 00:02:11.810
the KhrisKrafter's style is
much more straightforward.

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:18.690
Let's explore RTR, remove, turn,
and rehang with this style of garter bar.

00:02:18.723 --> 00:02:22.890
I have a bit of knitting on the machine
and I want to add a garter ridge,

00:02:22.923 --> 00:02:26.050
maybe for an accent or a turning row.

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:28.010
I have weight on the knitting.

00:02:28.043 --> 00:02:30.040
Now, this is important.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.040
I'll stop knitting with
the carriage on the right.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:41.170
First, I like to remove the working yarn
from the yarn feeder of the carriage.

00:02:41.203 --> 00:02:43.730
Now, if you forget to do this, no problem.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.170
I just like to make it a habit.

00:02:46.203 --> 00:02:50.370
I'll position the garter bar over
the needles, putting the hooks

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.730
in the slots of the bar.

00:02:52.763 --> 00:02:56.920
Notice that the perl side or the wrong or
the private side of the knitting

00:02:56.953 --> 00:03:00.040
is facing me right now.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.970
I'll slip the stitches to the bar and push
them all the way to the back of the bar.

00:03:05.003 --> 00:03:10.770
As you remove the stitches,
use the bar to open the latches.

00:03:10.803 --> 00:03:15.280
Once your knitting is off the machine,
pass your carriage to the opposite side

00:03:15.313 --> 00:03:19.810
of the needle bed so the working
yarn is in position to knit.

00:03:19.843 --> 00:03:24.120
Again, confirm that all
the latches are open.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.320
With the stitches pushed to the back
of the bar, before you turn and rehang

00:03:29.353 --> 00:03:34.320
the work, hook, notice
that there are little openings.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:40.090
We'll insert the hooks of the needles
in these openings to rehang the stitches.

00:03:40.123 --> 00:03:45.210
Now, turn the bar and your knitting
so the knit side is facing.

00:03:45.243 --> 00:03:51.850
To rehang the stitches, lay the bar flat,
positioning the hooks in those openings.

00:03:51.883 --> 00:03:57.330
Rotate the bar down and you can see
that the hooks are catching the stitches.

00:03:57.363 --> 00:04:00.330
If a latch is closed,
it's going to prevent the hooks

00:04:00.363 --> 00:04:02.920
from picking up that stitch.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:09.280
Pull down to slip the garter bar out
of the stitches and remove it completely.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.370
Check to see if any stitches have split or
are not in the hooks,

00:04:14.403 --> 00:04:18.440
and use a transfer tool
to manually repair them.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.410
Next, push the work back and knit a row.

00:04:22.443 --> 00:04:26.200
Notice the purl bumps facing you.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:32.490
To complete a garter row, we'll repeat
the steps and turn the work again.

00:04:32.523 --> 00:04:36.530
Remove the knitting from the machine,
turn the bar and the knitting,

00:04:36.563 --> 00:04:39.210
and re-hang it on the machine.

00:04:39.243 --> 00:04:44.010
This time, when I re-hung my work,
I remembered to use the needle stopper.

00:04:44.043 --> 00:04:47.450
If you have one, it can be really helpful.

00:04:47.483 --> 00:04:51.407
Once the stitches are back on the machine,
knit a few rows and admire

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.560
your single garter ridge.

